WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.153
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.453 --> 00:00:08.804
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:17.457
Unit eight: Part 4: Announcements, Voicemail and Ads. Today you will follow short talks and find the purpose, details and requests.

4
00:00:17.757 --> 00:00:20.433
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:24.669
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:26.460
Announcement.

7
00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.659
Announcement means a public message.

8
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.739
Listen to the announcement.

9
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.909
Your turn. Say: Announcement.

10
00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:38.803
Announcement.

11
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.516
Voicemail.

12
00:00:41.517 --> 00:00:43.899
Voicemail means a recorded phone message.

13
00:00:44.483 --> 00:00:45.891
She left a voicemail.

14
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:49.194
Your turn. Say: Voicemail.

15
00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.255
Voicemail.

16
00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:55.169
Advertisement.

17
00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:59.054
Advertisement means a message that promotes a product.

18
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.882
The advertisement offers a discount.

19
00:01:02.483 --> 00:01:05.507
Your turn. Say: Advertisement.

20
00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.600
Advertisement.

21
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.270
Discount.

22
00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:14.620
Discount means a reduction in price.

23
00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:17.065
Get a 20 percent discount.

24
00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:20.256
Your turn. Say: Discount.

25
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.043
Discount.

26
00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:25.703
Callback.

27
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:29.123
Callback means a return phone call.

28
00:01:29.717 --> 00:01:31.333
Please give me a callback.

29
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.186
Your turn. Say: Callback.

30
00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:38.023
Callback.

31
00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:39.761
Purpose.

32
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.028
Purpose means the reason for a message.

33
00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:45.372
What is the purpose of the call?

34
00:01:45.983 --> 00:01:48.299
Your turn. Say: Purpose.

35
00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.111
Purpose.

36
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:53.654
Limited.

37
00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.580
Limited means not unlimited.

38
00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.521
The offer is limited.

39
00:01:59.117 --> 00:02:01.653
Your turn. Say: Limited.

40
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.466
Limited.

41
00:02:06.217 --> 00:02:07.160
Reserve.

42
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.150
Reserve means to book in advance.

43
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.262
Reserve a seat today.

44
00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:15.804
Your turn. Say: Reserve.

45
00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:19.656
Reserve.

46
00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:24.268
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:27.058
Visal, what is Part 4?

48
00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:37.731
You hear a short talk by one speaker, such as an announcement, a recorded message or an advertisement, and answer three questions about it.

49
00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:41.165
What information is usually included?

50
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:52.742
The opening gives the purpose and the speaker. The middle gives details such as times, prices or problems. The ending gives a request or a next step.

51
00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.130
How should I listen?

52
00:02:56.217 --> 00:03:06.218
Preview the questions, listen for the purpose at the start, and catch numbers and names in the middle. The last sentence often tells you what the listener should do.

53
00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:08.786
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.275
Grammar focus: Strategy: purpose, details, request.

55
00:03:13.575 --> 00:03:14.785
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:18.110
This message is to remind you about your appointment.

57
00:03:19.017 --> 00:03:21.643
Please call us back before five o'clock today.

58
00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:29.235
Preview the questions, listen to the opening for the purpose, and catch the details. Always listen to the final request.

59
00:03:29.983 --> 00:03:33.495
Be careful! Don't say: I miss the request at the end.

60
00:03:35.433 --> 00:03:37.514
Say: I listen for the request.

61
00:03:37.814 --> 00:03:39.326
Last line matters.

62
00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:42.612
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.622
A Voicemail.

64
00:03:44.922 --> 00:03:47.885
A dentist's assistant leaves a voicemail for a patient.

65
00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.666
She says the purpose is to remind him about an appointment.

66
00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.991
The appointment is on Tuesday at nine o'clock.

67
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.091
She asks him to call back before five o'clock today.

68
00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.946
If he does not call, the office will give the time to another patient.

69
00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:08.896
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.622
Part 4 has blank speaker.

71
00:04:11.922 --> 00:04:15.088
A, three. B, five. C, one.

72
00:04:18.633 --> 00:04:20.552
The answer is C: one.

73
00:04:21.717 --> 00:04:23.623
The purpose is usually in the blank.

74
00:04:23.923 --> 00:04:28.320
A, opening. B, last number. C, title page.

75
00:04:31.867 --> 00:04:33.855
The answer is A: opening.

76
00:04:35.017 --> 00:04:36.296
When is the appointment?

77
00:04:36.596 --> 00:04:41.074
A, Friday at two. B, Tuesday at nine. C, Monday at ten.

78
00:04:44.633 --> 00:04:47.248
The answer is B: Tuesday at nine.

79
00:04:48.383 --> 00:04:49.907
What should the patient do?

80
00:04:50.207 --> 00:04:54.685
A, come at once. B, write a letter. C, call back before five.

81
00:04:58.233 --> 00:05:01.011
The answer is C: call back before five.

82
00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:04.417
The last sentence often gives a blank.

83
00:05:04.717 --> 00:05:08.173
A, request. B, title. C, joke.

84
00:05:11.733 --> 00:05:13.721
The answer is A: request.

85
00:05:14.933 --> 00:05:18.201
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.212
How do you answer questions about a talk?

87
00:05:30.017 --> 00:05:31.633
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:31.933 --> 00:05:44.933
I preview the three questions first. At the start of the talk I listen for the purpose, and in the middle I catch the numbers and names. At the end I listen for what the listener should do.

89
00:05:45.233 --> 00:05:46.942
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:52.975
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: purpose, details, request.

91
00:05:53.275 --> 00:05:57.309
Today's value is time management. Plan your day and use your time well.

92
00:05:57.609 --> 00:06:00.157
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

93
00:06:00.457 --> 00:06:03.284
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

